# Round XXIX Track C — graduated from known_gaps/. `.iter().enumerate()` over
# a Set now lowers correctly (fast-path gated on `collection_kind == Array` /
# `is_string_type`; non-Array receivers fall through to `lower_for_iterable`
# via synthetic-local substitution — see the sibling `vector_iter_enumerate`,
# `dict_iter_enumerate`, `iter_map_enumerate` fixtures for the axis coverage).
#
# History: was `KNOWN GAP: SetIter has 2 fields, the enumerate adapter reads
# field 2` — the exact spelling `E_EnumerateOnNonIterator`'s fix-it advice
# recommends. RED at HEAD (`gg build`) with:
#   `field index 2 out of range for SetIter__int64_t (has 2 fields)` (LIR
#   validator panic).
#
# `Set[T]` is insertion-ordered (D38) — indices are meaningful + deterministic.
int main():
    Set[int] s = {}
    s.add(7)
    s.add(8)
    for (i, x) in s.iter().enumerate():
        print(f"{i}->{x}")
    return 0
